MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_001: Hmm, I haven't seen Ninae anywhere. Where could\nshe be?
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_002: Ah! I recognize that black lace.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_003: *sigh*
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_004: She doesn't look busy...but I shouldn't interrupt,\njust in case.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_005: There's no rush. I'll just watch the clouds as I wait.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_006: Huh?
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_007: Lysander? How much time have you sat here?
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_008: Hehe. Judging by the sun, it's been quite a while\nsince I spotted you.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_009: So much sitting and so little saying things.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_010: You seemed lost in thought as usual. I didn't want\nto be a pest, so I waited.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_011: You left me be. Left me to my thoughts. Thank you.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_012: I was appreciating serenity. What is your suggestion\nthat I do instead?
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_013: I heard you were a chief celestial general, so I\nwanted to request a sparring match.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_014: You sat for that? For me? For a match? Hm.\nHow odd.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_015: Then spar we shall. But not here. At the place\nfor sparring.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_016: Really?! Thank you, Ninae!
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_030: 
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_017: Haaah... Haaah... I knew you wouldn't go easy on\nme. I'd ask for another round, but it's getting late.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_018: Sorry to keep you here so long. I was so focused on\nour training that time flew by.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_019: It flew past me too. I saw it go, but could not lower\nmy guard to catch it.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_020: I'm honored to hear that, Black-Lace Ninae.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_021: Again, you did me a favor sparring with me for\nso long.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_022: You needed to spar. But I must spar too. So the favor\nwas also done to myself.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_023: I'd like to be there the next time you train too.\nBut I'll be on my way now.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_024: Not yet. A favor for a favor.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_025: Mine is done, now we establish yours. Meet me\nwhere the sky is broad and open.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_026: Er, of course. But might I ask what you have in\nmind there?
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_027: You'll see when the time is right. When the favor\nis returned.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_028: Hmm. I think I know from experience where\nthis is headed.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_C_029: A private meeting, just the two of us... But no.\nShe's not the type...is she?
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_001: This is where Ninae asked me to meet her. But I still\ndon't know why.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_002: You arrived. Let us do nothing together.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_003: What? Is that all?
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_004: Not "all." Nothing. I have fond memories of doing\nnothing with my father. Now we will do it too.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_005: Oh! I see now. So that was the role you brought me\nhere to play.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_006: I appreciate the invitation, but I'm a bit young to\nbe a stand-in for anyone's father.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_007: But you look lovingly—longingly—at the sky.\nThat love and longing is why I asked.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_008: H-how did you know about that?!
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_009: My eyes told me. My eyes saw your eyes, and the\npassion in them as they saw the sky.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_010: I...I see. It's a little embarrassing to hear it put\nso bluntly.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_011: Then I may as well admit that my hobby is lying in\nthe meadow and looking up at the sky.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_012: Someday, I want to be a knight who soars through\nthe skies. It's been a dream of mine since childhood.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_013: Even when I'm soaring over the battlefield, I find the\nvastness of the sky deeply moving.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_014: The skies are wonderful. They go on forever into\nthe infinite. Into freedom.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_015: Exactly. I'm glad you understand.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_016: I was afraid people would laugh if they knew I had\nsuch an idle hobby. So I usually don't talk about it.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_017: I wouldn't laugh. I like to do nothing just like you do.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_018: Heh. It's nice to know someone else feels the\nsame way.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_019: Now then, shall we spend the rest of the day doing\nnothing together?
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_020: Yes. Mm.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_021: Ahhh. Is it evening already? I had a nice\ntime today.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_022: I would love to continue, but I ought to be getting\nback soon.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_023: Shh. Don't leave yet. Don't do something in our time\nof doing nothing.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_024: Er...but I need to get back to my training. Otherwise\nI'll never improve.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_025: Training? I'll train you later. So stay now.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_026: Er...alright, I suppose. Just for a little while.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_027: Thank you. Your doing nothing is doing me\na kindness.
MID_SE_Nin_Lys_B_028: Uh-oh... My heart skipped a beat there. Best be\ncareful not to get too involved.